{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports warehouse office desktop not connecting to the network; checking account status, devices, and usual hours."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0108",
  "reason": "Ticket sender's desktop reportedly not connecting to the network; checking online state, last check-in, and warnings."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Our records show your desktop (BL-DT-0108) is currently offline and hasn't checked in since the last sign-in window, so it isn't reaching the network. While you wait for the help desk, please try these: shut the desktop down fully and power it back on, check that the network cable is firmly plugged into both the desktop and the wall port (or, if you use Wi-Fi, turn Wi-Fi off and on), and let us know whether any other computers near you in the warehouse office are also offline. Your ticket has been passed to a senior technician because the desktop is offline and we need to find the cause before your shift starts.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: James O'Connor (user 8, Operations, Warehouse Supervisor), account active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, 0 failed logins, usual hours 06:00-14:00 America/Chicago. Note: triage marked user_blocked true, but the account record shows sign-in is not blocked, so I did not act on that flag. Checked device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro, assigned to James): offline, last check-in 2026-10-11T00:57:45Z, disk 78% free, no warnings. Per KB-014, an offline status confirms no path to the internet, so the fault is at the device or the office network path. Shared the basic KB-014 fixes with the user (restart, wired connection, Wi-Fi toggle). I could not confirm whether other warehouse office devices are affected, which is the KB-014 escalation trigger, so I escalated to Tier 2 for physical/network investigation at the warehouse office. No password, unlock, or block actions were taken.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
